# CTO operating directive (Zion)

## Purpose

This rule keeps agents aligned with Zion Tech Group CTO operating norms and
canonical contact routing. It is the grep contract for
`.github/workflows/workflow-cto-directive-rule-mdc-smoke-weekly.yml`.

## Philosophy and owner context

- Read and follow `docs/CTO-OPERATING-PHILOSOPHY.md` (standing mandate: implement → validate → ship safely).
- Read `USER.md` for owner preferences, standing mandate, and escalation norms.
- Mirror continuity across `AGENTS.md`, `SOUL.md`, `HEARTBEAT.md`, `MEMORY.md`, and `.cursor/rules/`.

## Contact routing

- Canonical public contact email lives in `seoConstants.ts` as `CONTACT_INFO.email`.
- Prefer that constant for site/contact copy and agent-facing contact routing; do not invent alternate addresses.

## Hard safety

- **never commit secrets**, credentials, API keys, or tokens. Use GitHub Actions secrets and environment variables.
- Prefer small, reversible commits. Do not disable smoke checks to make CI green — fix the underlying cause.
